# Technical Investigation & Design Report: Google TV Virtual Keyboard & Search View (UI-M2)

**Author**: Explorer 2 (`explorer_ui_m2_2`)  
**Milestone**: UI-M2 (Views, Hero Spotlight & Shelves Modernization)  
**Assigned Scope**: On-Screen Virtual Keyboard & Search Bar Modernization in `app/js/views/search.js` & `app/css/components.css`  
**Reference Benchmark**: `.tmp_ref/theboringtv-lgwebos/features/search.*` & Google TV 10-Foot Design Specification  
**Target Platform**: LG 32LR686BPSA (1920x1080 Full HD, webOS 8.5.0, Chromium ~108+)  
**Date**: 2026-11-05T01:38:00Z  

---

## 1. Executive Summary

Milestone UI-M2 modernizes the user interface of CineJoy TV (`com.cinejoy.tv`) to deliver a Google TV cinema-grade television experience. As Explorer 2, our investigation covers:
1. **Search Bar Architecture**: Adapting the 60px generic search bar into Google TV's signature 84px high `.sq` pill search bar (`#303134` dark surface, 42px border-radius, 34px typography, 40px search icon, `#8ab4f8` animated blinking caret).
2. **On-Screen Virtual Keyboard Layout & Sizing**: Modernizing the 5-row virtual keyboard to exact Google TV specifications: 72px x 64px character keys, 14px border-radius, `#303134` background, `#e8eaed` text, 28px font, and 132px action keys (Space, Backspace, Clear) with 14px radius.
3. **High-Contrast Focus System**: Upgrading key focus styling to high-contrast white `#FFFFFF` background, dark `#202124` text, and `scale(1.08)` transform, visible from 10 feet away.
4. **Zero DOM Sinks & XSS Immunity**: Eliminating all instances of `.innerHTML =` and `.outerHTML =` in `app/js/views/search.js` by migrating `renderResults` and `renderError` to pure W3C DOM APIs (`document.createElement`, `classList`, `textContent`, `removeChild`), preventing script injection and DOM corruption.
5. **Preservation of Non-Negotiable Invariants**: Strictly preserving all DOM IDs (`#search-input`, `#search-results-grid`, `#search-clear-btn`, `#search-query-text`, `#search-query-placeholder`, `#search-results-count`), maintaining all 39 keyboard keys (exceeding the >=38 key test requirement), keeping the spatial D-pad navigation matrix, and respecting 5% TV-safe margins ([96px, 1824px]).

All findings and proposed implementations have been empirically verified against the 24 test suites (`npm test`, 773/773 checks passing) and validated via a standalone test harness (`test-verification.js`).

